## 2. Trust boundaries (security)

| Boundary | Source | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| HTTP request body/params | User | Every route validates via arktype or manual checks before DB/AI |
| URL path params (`[id]`, `[chatId]`) | User | Coerced with `Number()` + `Number.isInteger()` guards |
| Cookie (`sl_session`) | User-controlled bytes | Signed HMAC; middleware + `requireUser` re-validate against DB |
| LLM output (Groq) | Untrusted | Rendered as JSX text only; KaTeX escapes; control-line parser strips markers |
| Source excerpts (RAG) | Untrusted data | Delimited + explicitly marked untrusted in system prompt |
| YouTube transcripts / PDF text | Untrusted | Ingested as text; chunked into FTS5 |
| Environment vars | Operator | Validated at boot (`validateRuntimeEnv`) in production |
| External fetch (Groq) | Outbound | Single allowlisted host, no user-supplied URLs |

Key security controls already in place:

- **Parameterized SQL everywhere** (repo.ts uses `?` placeholders; no string interpolation of user input). `deleteUser` uses sub-select filters, not user input.
- **Passwords:** scrypt (N=2^15, r=8, p=1, maxmem 128MB), salted, with transparent rehash from legacy params. Min length 10 (enforced at signup/change-password; login has no min so existing users can sign in).
- **Sessions:** httpOnly, secure in prod, sameSite lax, signed cookie (HMAC-SHA256 via WebCrypto, edge-safe). Revocation immediate via DB lookup. 7-day TTL.
- **Secrets at rest:** BYO LLM keys encrypted AES-256-GCM with scrypt-derived key (v2), v1 legacy decrypt supported. `ENCRYPTION_SECRET` required in prod.
- **Login throttling:** DB-backed, per-account (10/15min) + per-IP (30/15min); unknown emails get a dummy hash to equalize timing; disabled accounts return same error either way.
- **Headers:** CSP (self + unsafe-inline scripts, no eval in prod), HSTS (2yr), X-Frame-Options DENY, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy. Set in `next.config.ts` for all paths.
- **Proxy-aware client IP:** `TRUST_PROXY_HOPS` reads from the trusted end of X-Forwarded-For.
- **Security headers on every route** including API (Next `headers()` applies to `/:path*`).
- **No secrets in logs:** provider error text logged server-side only, generic message to client. No `console.log` of keys/passwords/tokens found.
- **No `eval()` usage.** `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` only in three places, all reviewed:
  - `Markdown.tsx` KaTeX output (sanitized by KaTeX with `trust: false`) — documented.
  - `AppShell.tsx` exit-animation snapshot (client-captured already-rendered DOM, not user input) — low risk but note.
  - `icons.tsx` glyph (static icon markup) — low risk.
- **XSS posture:** React auto-escaping for all user/AI content. Markdown renderer never injects raw HTML. URLs render as plain text.
- **Prompt injection mitigation:** excerpts delimited, marked untrusted, model instructed to ignore instructions inside them (lowers risk, does not remove it — per PR notes).
- **Resource limits:** ≤100 notebooks/user, ≤100 sources/notebook (enforced in ingest). Source text cap 2MB. Question max 2000 chars. Chat history trimmed to 6000 chars.
- **Rate limits:** DB-backed, per user, for LLM/expensive routes (chat 150/hr, generate 30/hr, ingest 20/hr, youtube 10/hr, signup, change-password).
- **Authorization:** every protected route calls `requireUser`/`requireAdmin`; ownership checked via `ownNotebook`/`ownConversation` (returns 404 for foreign/missing to avoid existence oracle).
- **Cascade deletes:** notebooks → sources/chunks/cards/conversations/messages; users → notebooks.
- **Dependency audit:** vitest upgraded for tinypool advisory; `.opencode/` untracked.

Known gaps / things to watch (from PR notes + review):

- `postcss` advisory via Next (needs Next 16, breaking).
- `public/mock/index.html` still loads Google Fonts; CSP blocks them there (cosmetic).
- Account lockout: attacker who knows an email can lock it 15 min (trade-off).
- `AppShell.tsx` captures `el.innerHTML` for transition animation — ensure it never captures unsanitized content (it captures rendered DOM, but review if any user-controlled HTML ever lands in `.screen`).
- No CSRF token beyond sameSite=lax cookies (acceptable for same-origin API, but review if cross-site POSTs become a concern).
- `TRUST_PROXY_HOPS` unset defaults to trusting leftmost XFF entry — spoofable behind non-Vercel proxies; document for deployers.
- `ENCRYPTION_SECRET` fallback to insecure dev secret in non-prod; boot validation only in prod. Ensure prod always sets it.
- Health endpoint (`/api/health`) runs `SELECT 1` with no auth — fine for liveness, but consider not exposing DB errors.
- `reset-demo` / admin endpoints: verify admin gating (spot-check `requireAdmin`).
- No request body size limit beyond Next defaults; large PDF text capped at 2MB client-side extraction, but server accepts up to 2MB text.
- LLM key never returned to client (only `hasPersonalKey` boolean) — good.
- `dummyHash` cached globally; fine.

